  "reviewers": {
    "aesthetic": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "blocking_issues": [],
      "non_blocking_notes": [
        "R4 no longer reads as a flat ceiling disk in the underside view. The 280mm deep tapered opal body, smaller lower opening, external bronze arch, and separate side supports establish a clear hanging lantern silhouette.",
        "The single side arch reads as an external structural element rather than a handle sitting on a flat diffuser. Its attachment points and outward separation are visible in the underside, closeup, and side views.",
        "The conical body gives the fixture a stronger vertical profile while preserving a broad 780mm upper diffuser opening and a 520mm lower opening. This creates a clear light-mid-century proportion at the approximately 1m overall scale.",
        "The context view shows the fixture as a distinct living-room focal point above the seating zone. It remains visually independent from the dining table and does not create a table-centered composition.",
        "The three bronze support rods and side arch introduce a mild lantern/cage character. The current version remains controlled because the structure uses one arch and limited supports, but the rods should remain thin and matte in any product interpretation.",
        "The white tapered body is visually substantial, but the 350mm drop and open lower profile prevent it from feeling like a heavy ceiling box. The black HVAC band remains a separate linear layer beneath it."
      ],
